IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa14-nouns`

-- coa14-ch07-premiums.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapter 7 "Share premiums", ss 610 to 616 (lines 8206-8279).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Every rule cites its provision with @ref and quotes it (-- src: lines).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). A decision function answers MAYBE:
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE: the text says yes / no in its own words ("means", "if", "where", a flat negative);
--     every JUST FALSE branch carries   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING: the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text,
--     limited by its own wording); every such branch carries   -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- SEAMS (PLAN.md section 4): a fact another part answers is an INPUT named for the section that answers it
-- (for example `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company`).

§ `Chapter 7 -- Share premiums`

§§ `s 610 Application of share premiums`

-- src:8209 | (1) If a company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise, a sum equal to the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares must be transferred to an account called “the share premium account”.
@ref s 610(1) Application of share premiums (src:8209)
GIVEN `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(1) the company must transfer a sum to the share premium account` MEANS
    IF `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company issues shares at a premium"

-- The sum is "equal to the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares". What a premium is, and how a
-- non-cash premium is valued, the text does not say (undefined term): the aggregate is an input.
-- src:8209 | (1) If a company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise, a sum equal to the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares must be transferred to an account called “the share premium account”.
@ref s 610(1) Application of share premiums: the sum (src:8209)
GIVEN `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 610(1) the sum that must be transferred to the share premium account` MEANS
    IF `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise`
    THEN JUST `the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company issues shares at a premium" gives a sum only for shares issued at a premium

-- src:8210 | (2) Where, on issuing shares, a company has transferred a sum to the share premium account, it may use that sum to write off—
-- src:8211 | (a) the expenses of the issue of those shares;
-- src:8212 | (b) any commission paid on the issue of those shares.
@ref s 610(2) Application of share premiums: write-offs (src:8210-8212)
GIVEN `on issuing shares the company has transferred a sum to the share premium account` IS A BOOLEAN
      use IS A `s 610(2) use of the sum in the share premium account`
      `the item relates to the issue of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(2) the company may use the sum to write off the item` MEANS
    IF `on issuing shares the company has transferred a sum to the share premium account`
    THEN CONSIDER use
         WHEN `s 610(2)(a) writing off the expenses of the issue of those shares` THEN
             IF `the item relates to the issue of those shares`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for expenses "of the issue of those shares"
         WHEN `s 610(2)(b) writing off any commission paid on the issue of those shares` THEN
             IF `the item relates to the issue of those shares`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for commission "paid on the issue of those shares"
         WHEN `s 610(2) some other use of the sum` THEN
             NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names (a) and (b) and does not say "only"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on issuing shares, a company has transferred a sum to the share premium account"

-- src:8213 | (3) The company may use the share premium account to pay up new shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares.
@ref s 610(3) Application of share premiums: bonus shares (src:8213)
GIVEN `the shares are new shares to be allotted to members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are to be allotted as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(3) the company may use the share premium account to pay up the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are new shares to be allotted to members` AND `they are to be allotted as fully paid bonus shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "new shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares"

-- src:8214 | (4) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), the provisions of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital apply as if the share premium account were part of its paid up share capital.
@ref s 610(4) Application of share premiums: the reduction provisions (src:8214)
GIVEN `the account is used as subsection (2) or (3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(4) the reduction provisions treat the share premium account as paid up share capital` MEANS
    IF `the account is used as subsection (2) or (3) allows`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsections (2) and (3)" the use there allowed is outside this rule
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8215 | (5) This section has effect subject to—
-- src:8216 | section 611 (group reconstruction relief);
-- src:8217 | section 612 (merger relief);
-- src:8218 | section 614 (power to make further provisions by regulations).
@ref s 610(5) Application of share premiums: subject to ss 611, 612 and 614 (src:8215-8218)
GIVEN `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares` IS A NUMBER
      `s 611(2) the issuing company is not required to transfer any amount in excess of the minimum premium value` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 611(3) the minimum premium value` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 612(2) section 610 does not apply to the premiums on those shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a regulation under section 614 relieves the company from the requirements of section 610` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 610(5) the sum that must be transferred to the share premium account, subject to sections 611, 612 and 614` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 610(1) gives a sum only "If a company issues shares at a premium"
        IF `a regulation under section 614 relieves the company from the requirements of section 610`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations under s 614 are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE `the sum after any relief`
    WHERE
        premiums MEANS `the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares`
        `the sum after any relief` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 611(2) the issuing company is not required to transfer any amount in excess of the minimum premium value`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether s 611 relieves the company is not known
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                CONSIDER `s 611(3) the minimum premium value`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 611(4) leaves the base value undefined where the assets do not exceed the liabilities
                WHEN JUST mpv THEN IF mpv LESS THAN premiums THEN JUST mpv ELSE JUST premiums
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
                CONSIDER `s 612(2) section 610 does not apply to the premiums on those shares`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether s 612 relieves the company is not known
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST 0
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST premiums

-- src:8219 | (6) In this Chapter “the issuing company” means the company issuing shares as mentioned in subsection (1) above.
@ref s 610(6) Application of share premiums: "the issuing company" (src:8219)
GIVEN `the company is issuing shares as mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(6) the company is the issuing company` MEANS
    IF `the company is issuing shares as mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the issuing company” means the company issuing shares as mentioned in subsection (1) above"

§§ `s 611 Group reconstruction relief`

-- A nominee counts: s 616(2)(b) extends "the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company"
-- to a nominee of that company, and its last sentence reads the reference to "the transferor company" accordingly.
-- src:8222 | (1) This section applies where the issuing company—
-- src:8223 | (a) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company (“the holding company”), and
-- src:8224 | (b) allots shares—
-- src:8225 | (i) to the holding company, or
-- src:8226 | (ii) to another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company,
-- src:8227 | in consideration for the transfer to the issuing company of non-cash assets of a company (“the transferor company”) that is a member of the group of companies that comprises the holding company and all its wholly-owned subsidiaries.
@ref s 611(1) Group reconstruction relief: when the section applies (src:8222-8227)
GIVEN `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted to the holding company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted to a nominee of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted to another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted to a nominee of another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1163(1) the asset is a non-cash asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted in consideration for the transfer to the issuing company of non-cash assets of the transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor company is a member of the group of companies that comprises the holding company and all its wholly-owned subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 611(1) section 611 applies` MEANS
    IF       `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company`
         AND (   `s 616(2) the act is treated as an act of the company` `s 616(2)(b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company` `the shares are allotted to the holding company itself` `the shares are allotted to a nominee of the holding company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              OR `s 616(2) the act is treated as an act of the company` `s 616(2)(b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company` `the shares are allotted to another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company itself` `the shares are allotted to a nominee of another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND `s 1163(1) the asset is a non-cash asset`
         AND `the shares are allotted in consideration for the transfer to the issuing company of non-cash assets of the transferor company`
         AND `the transferor company is a member of the group of companies that comprises the holding company and all its wholly-owned subsidiaries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the issuing company— (a) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company ..., and (b) allots shares ..."

-- src:8228 | (2) Where the shares in the issuing company allotted in consideration for the transfer are issued at a premium, the issuing company is not required by section 610 to transfer any amount in excess of the minimum premium value to the share premium account.
@ref s 611(2) Group reconstruction relief: the limit on the amount transferred (src:8228)
GIVEN `s 611(1) section 611 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the shares allotted in consideration for the transfer are issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 611(2) the issuing company is not required to transfer any amount in excess of the minimum premium value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 611(1) section 611 applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the shares allotted in consideration for the transfer are issued at a premium`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether s 611(1) applies is not known
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the shares ... are issued at a premium"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the issuing company"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the shares allotted in consideration for the transfer are issued at a premium`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the shares in the issuing company allotted in consideration for the transfer are issued at a premium"

-- "(if any)": where the base value of the consideration does not exceed the aggregate nominal value there is no amount, read as 0 (fork).
-- src:8229 | (3) The minimum premium value means the amount (if any) by which the base value of the consideration for the shares allotted exceeds the aggregate nominal value of the shares.
@ref s 611(3) Group reconstruction relief: the minimum premium value (src:8229)
GIVEN `s 611(4) the base value of the consideration for the shares allotted` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the aggregate nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 611(3) the minimum premium value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 611(4) the base value of the consideration for the shares allotted`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 611(4) gives no base value where the assets transferred do not exceed the liabilities assumed
    WHEN JUST base THEN
        IF base GREATER THAN `the aggregate nominal value of the shares`
        THEN JUST (base MINUS `the aggregate nominal value of the shares`)
        ELSE JUST 0 -- the text says "the amount (if any)": no amount is read as 0 (fork F-minpremium)

-- src:8230 | (4) The base value of the consideration for the shares allotted is the amount by which the base value of the assets transferred exceeds the base value of any liabilities of the transferor company assumed by the issuing company as part of the consideration for the assets transferred.
@ref s 611(4) Group reconstruction relief: the base value of the consideration (src:8230)
GIVEN `the base value of the assets transferred` IS A NUMBER
      `the base value of any liabilities of the transferor company assumed by the issuing company as part of the consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 611(4) the base value of the consideration for the shares allotted` MEANS
    IF `the base value of the assets transferred` GREATER THAN `the base value of any liabilities of the transferor company assumed by the issuing company as part of the consideration`
    THEN JUST (`the base value of the assets transferred` MINUS `the base value of any liabilities of the transferor company assumed by the issuing company as part of the consideration`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the amount by which the base value of the assets transferred exceeds" presupposes an excess and the text gives none otherwise

-- src:8232 | (a) the base value of assets transferred is taken as—
-- src:8233 | (i) the cost of those assets to the transferor company, or
-- src:8234 | (ii) if less, the amount at which those assets are stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer;
@ref s 611(5)(a) Group reconstruction relief: the base value of the assets transferred (src:8232-8234)
GIVEN `the cost of those assets to the transferor company` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount at which those assets are stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 611(5)(a) the base value of the assets transferred` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount at which those assets are stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the cost of those assets to the transferor company` -- limb (ii) needs a stated amount: without one the cost is the base value
    WHEN JUST stated THEN
        IF stated LESS THAN `the cost of those assets to the transferor company`
        THEN stated -- limb (ii) "if less"
        ELSE `the cost of those assets to the transferor company` -- limb (i)

-- src:8235 | (b) the base value of the liabilities assumed is taken as the amount at which they are stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer.
@ref s 611(5)(b) Group reconstruction relief: the base value of the liabilities assumed (src:8235)
GIVEN `the amount at which the liabilities are stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 611(5)(b) the base value of the liabilities assumed` MEANS
    `the amount at which the liabilities are stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer`

§§ `s 612 Merger relief`

-- src:8237 | (1) This section applies where the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in another company in pursuance of an arrangement providing for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration for the shares allotted is to be provided—
-- src:8238 | (a) by the issue or transfer to the issuing company of equity shares in the other company, or
-- src:8239 | (b) by the cancellation of any such shares not held by the issuing company.
@ref s 612(1) Merger relief: when the section applies (src:8237-8239)
GIVEN `s 613 the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in the other company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement provides for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to the issuing company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to a nominee of the issuing company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any such shares not held by the issuing company are cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(1) section 612 applies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the arrangement provides for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company`
            AND (   `s 616(2) the act is treated as an act of the company` `s 616(2)(b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company` `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to the issuing company itself` `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to a nominee of the issuing company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 OR `any such shares not held by the issuing company are cancelled`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... an arrangement providing for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration ... is to be provided— (a) ... or (b) ..."
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 613 the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in the other company`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the 90% equity holding was secured is not known
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in another company"

-- src:8245 | (4) This section does not apply in a case falling within section 611 (group reconstruction relief).
@ref s 612(4) Merger relief: not a case within section 611 (src:8245)
GIVEN `s 611(1) section 611 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(4) section 612 applies to the case, so far as section 611 is concerned` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 611(1) section 611 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in a case falling within section 611"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the carve-out names only cases within section 611; section 612(1) decides the rest
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the case falls within section 611 is not known

-- The two answers together (E1 option B: gathered by hand, named for both sections). The carve-out of s 612(4) answers
-- NOTHING for a case that is not within section 611 (it names only cases within s 611), so the gather reads the section 611
-- answer as well: a case that is not within s 611 is left to s 612(1).
-- src:8237 | (1) This section applies where the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in another company in pursuance of an arrangement providing for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration for the shares allotted is to be provided—
-- src:8238 | (a) by the issue or transfer to the issuing company of equity shares in the other company, or
-- src:8239 | (b) by the cancellation of any such shares not held by the issuing company.
--
-- src:8245 | (4) This section does not apply in a case falling within section 611 (group reconstruction relief).
@ref s 612(1) and (4) Merger relief: whether section 612 applies to the case (src:8237-8239 src:8245)
GIVEN `s 611(1) section 611 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 612(1) section 612 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(1) and (4) section 612 applies to the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 612(4) section 612 applies to the case, so far as section 611 is concerned` `s 611(1) section 611 applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in a case falling within section 611"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 612(1) section 612 applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `s 611(1) section 611 applies`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 612(1) section 612 applies` -- not within section 611: section 612(1) decides
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): unreachable, section 612(4) answers JUST FALSE for a case within section 611
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `s 612(1) section 612 applies`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding"
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the case falls within section 611 is not known
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): neither answer is known

-- src:8240 | (2) If the equity shares in the issuing company allotted in pursuance of the arrangement in consideration for the acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in the other company are issued at a premium, section 610 does not apply to the premiums on those shares.
@ref s 612(2) Merger relief: section 610 does not apply to the premiums (src:8240)
GIVEN `s 612(1) and (4) section 612 applies to the case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the shares are equity shares in the issuing company allotted in pursuance of the arrangement in consideration for the acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in the other company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(2) section 610 does not apply to the premiums on those shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 612(1) and (4) section 612 applies to the case`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 612 applies is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the shares are equity shares in the issuing company allotted in pursuance of the arrangement in consideration for the acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in the other company` AND `they are issued at a premium`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the equity shares ... are issued at a premium"

-- src:8241 | (3) Where the arrangement also provides for the allotment of any shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration for those shares is to be provided—
-- src:8242 | (a) by the issue or transfer to the issuing company of non-equity shares in the other company, or
-- src:8243 | (b) by the cancellation of any such shares in that company not held by the issuing company,
-- src:8244 | relief under subsection (2) extends to any shares in the issuing company allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement.
@ref s 612(3) Merger relief: extension to other shares (src:8241-8244)
GIVEN `s 612(1) and (4) section 612 applies to the case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement also provides for the allotment of shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration is provided by the issue or transfer to the issuing company of non-equity shares in the other company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement also provides for the allotment of shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration is provided by the cancellation of any such shares in the other company not held by the issuing company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(3) the relief under subsection (2) extends to the shares` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT provides
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the arrangement also provides for the allotment of any shares ... on terms that the consideration ... is to be provided— (a) ... or (b) ..."
        IF NOT `the shares are allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relief under subsection (2) extends to any shares in the issuing company allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement" (fork F-612-3)
        OTHERWISE relief
    WHERE
        provides MEANS
            `the arrangement also provides for the allotment of shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration is provided by the issue or transfer to the issuing company of non-equity shares in the other company`
            OR `the arrangement also provides for the allotment of shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration is provided by the cancellation of any such shares in the other company not held by the issuing company`
        relief MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 612(1) and (4) section 612 applies to the case`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 612 applies is not known
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "relief under subsection (2)" exists only where this section applies
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `s 613 Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding`

-- Lead-in, s 613(1): "The following provisions have effect to determine for the purposes of section 612 ..." (a signpost: inert, fork F-signpost).

-- (3)(a): it is immaterial whether any of those shares were acquired in pursuance of the arrangement. The holdings in the
-- class records count whichever way they were acquired; this function states the rule so that it is tested on both sides.
-- src:8250 | (a) it is immaterial whether any of those shares were acquired in pursuance of the arrangement; and
@ref s 613(3)(a) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding: how the shares were acquired is immaterial (src:8250)
GIVEN `the shares were acquired in pursuance of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 613(3)(a) the shares count towards company A's holding` MEANS
    IF `the shares were acquired in pursuance of the arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- the text says it is "immaterial": both ways they count

-- src:8251 | (b) shares in company B held by the company as treasury shares are excluded in determining the nominal value of company B's share capital.
@ref s 613(3)(b) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding: treasury shares are excluded (src:8251)
GIVEN class IS A `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 613(3)(b) the nominal value of the class counted in company B's equity share capital` MEANS
    class's `s 613(2) nominal value of the class in company B's equity share capital, treasury shares included`
        MINUS class's `s 613(3)(b) nominal value of the class held by company B as treasury shares`

-- src:8253 | (5) For the purposes of this section shares held by—
-- src:8254 | (a) a company that is company A's holding company or subsidiary, or
-- src:8255 | (b) a subsidiary of company A's holding company, or
-- src:8256 | (c) its or their nominees,
-- src:8257 | are treated as held by company A.
@ref s 613(5) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding: shares treated as held by company A (src:8253-8257)
GIVEN class IS A `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 613(5) the nominal value of the class treated as held by company A` MEANS
        class's `s 613(2) nominal value of the equity shares of the class that company A holds`
    PLUS class's `s 613(5)(a) nominal value of the class held by a company that is company A's holding company or subsidiary`
    PLUS class's `s 613(5)(b) nominal value of the class held by a subsidiary of company A's holding company`
    PLUS class's `s 613(5)(c) nominal value of the class held by the nominees of those companies`

-- src:8248 | (2) Company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B if in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B (in pursuance of that arrangement) it holds equity shares in company B of an aggregate amount equal to 90% or more of the nominal value of that company's equity share capital.
@ref s 613(2) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding (src:8248)
GIVEN `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      classes IS A LIST OF `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 613(2) company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B (in pursuance of that arrangement) it holds"
        IF capital AT MOST 0
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no nominal value of equity share capital to measure 90% of
        IF held TIMES 100 AT LEAST 90 TIMES capital
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... it holds equity shares in company B of an aggregate amount equal to 90% or more of the nominal value of that company's equity share capital"
    WHERE
        capital MEANS sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 613(3)(b) the nominal value of the class counted in company B's equity share capital` c) classes)
        held MEANS sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 613(5) the nominal value of the class treated as held by company A` c) classes)

-- src:8252 | (4) Where the equity share capital of company B is divided into different classes of shares, company A is not regarded as having secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B unless the requirements of subsection (2) are met in relation to each of those classes of shares taken separately.
@ref s 613(4) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding: each class taken separately (src:8252)
GIVEN `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      classes IS A LIST OF `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 613(4) the class requirement bars company A from being regarded as having secured the holding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF count classes AT MOST 1
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar arises only "Where the equity share capital of company B is divided into different classes of shares"
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST FALSE) results
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirements of subsection (2) are not met in relation to a class taken separately
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS NOTHING) results
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a class has no nominal value to measure 90% of
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the requirements of subsection (2) are met in relation to each of those classes taken separately" (the unless is met)
    WHERE
        results MEANS map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 613(2) company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B` `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` (LIST c)) classes

-- E1 option B, gathered by hand: (2) and (4) together.
-- src:8248 | (2) Company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B if in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B (in pursuance of that arrangement) it holds equity shares in company B of an aggregate amount equal to 90% or more of the nominal value of that company's equity share capital.
--
-- src:8252 | (4) Where the equity share capital of company B is divided into different classes of shares, company A is not regarded as having secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B unless the requirements of subsection (2) are met in relation to each of those classes of shares taken separately.
@ref s 613(2) and (4) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding: both rules together (src:8248 src:8252)
GIVEN `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      classes IS A LIST OF `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 613(2) and (4) company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B, each class taken separately` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 613(4) the class requirement bars company A from being regarded as having secured the holding` `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` classes
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "company A is not regarded as having secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B unless"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 613(2) company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B` `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` classes
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `s 613(2) company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B` `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of that arrangement` classes
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B if ... 90% or more"
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a class could not be measured
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is nothing to measure

§§ `s 614 Power to make further provision by regulations`

-- Inert (machinery, reason 2): a regulation-making power. Its effect on s 610 appears only as the input
-- `a regulation under section 614 relieves the company from the requirements of section 610` of s 610(5).

§§ `s 615 Relief may be reflected in company's balance sheet`

-- src:8264 | An amount corresponding to the amount representing the premiums, or part of the premiums, on shares issued by a company that by virtue of any relief under this Chapter is not included in the company's share premium account may also be disregarded in determining the amount at which any shares or other consideration provided for the shares issued is to be included in the company's balance sheet.
@ref s 615 Relief may be reflected in company's balance sheet (src:8264)
GIVEN `the premiums are not included in the share premium account by virtue of relief under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount representing those premiums` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 615 the amount that may be disregarded in determining the balance sheet amount` MEANS
    IF `the premiums are not included in the share premium account by virtue of relief under this Chapter`
    THEN JUST `the amount representing those premiums`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is for premiums that "by virtue of any relief under this Chapter" are not in the account

§§ `s 616 Interpretation of this Chapter`

-- src:8268 | “arrangement” means any agreement, scheme or arrangement (including an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with—
-- src:8269 | (a) Part 26 or 26A (arrangements and reconstructions), or
-- src:8270 | (b) section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)) (liquidator in winding up accepting shares as consideration for sale of company property));
@ref s 616(1) Interpretation of this Chapter: "arrangement" (src:8268-8270)
GIVEN `it is an agreement, scheme or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sanctioned in accordance with section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(1) the thing is an arrangement` MEANS
    IF `it is an agreement, scheme or arrangement` OR `it was sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A` OR `it was sanctioned in accordance with section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“arrangement” means any agreement, scheme or arrangement (including ...)"

-- src:8271 | “company”, except in reference to the issuing company, includes any body corporate;
@ref s 616(1) Interpretation of this Chapter: "company" (src:8271)
GIVEN `the reference is to the issuing company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(1) the body is a company for this Chapter` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to the issuing company`
    THEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in reference to the issuing company" the word keeps its section 1 meaning, which the keel answers
    ELSE IF `the body is a body corporate`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE `s 1(1) the body is a company` -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes any body corporate" does not say a body that is not a body corporate is not a company

-- src:8272 | “equity shares” means shares comprised in a company's equity share capital, and “non-equity shares” means shares (of any class) that are not so comprised;
@ref s 616(1) Interpretation of this Chapter: "equity shares" and "non-equity shares" (src:8272)
GIVEN `s 548 the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(1) the shares are equity shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 548 the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“equity shares” means shares comprised in a company's equity share capital"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "equity share capital" is defined by s 548 (coa13)

-- src:8272 | “equity shares” means shares comprised in a company's equity share capital, and “non-equity shares” means shares (of any class) that are not so comprised;
@ref s 616(1) Interpretation of this Chapter: "non-equity shares" (src:8272)
GIVEN `s 548 the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(1) the shares are non-equity shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 548 the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non-equity shares” means shares (of any class) that are not so comprised"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "equity share capital" is defined by s 548 (coa13)

-- src:8273 | “the issuing company” has the meaning given by section 610(6).
@ref s 616(1) Interpretation of this Chapter: "the issuing company" (src:8273)
GIVEN `the company is issuing shares as mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(1) the company is the issuing company` MEANS
    `s 610(6) the company is the issuing company` `the company is issuing shares as mentioned in subsection (1)`

-- src:8274 | (2) References in this Chapter (however expressed) to—
-- src:8275 | (a) the acquisition by a company of shares in another company, and
-- src:8276 | (b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company,
-- src:8277 | include (respectively) the acquisition of shares by, and the issue or allotment or transfer of shares to or by, a nominee of that company.
@ref s 616(2) Interpretation of this Chapter: references include acts of a nominee (src:8274-8277)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 616(2) kind of act`
      `the act is done by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is done by a nominee of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(2) the act is treated as an act of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 616(2)(a) the acquisition by a company of shares in another company` THEN
        IF `the act is done by the company itself` OR `the act is done by a nominee of that company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include (respectively) the acquisition of shares by ... a nominee of that company" extends the reference and says nothing of other persons
    WHEN `s 616(2)(b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company` THEN
        IF `the act is done by the company itself` OR `the act is done by a nominee of that company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include ... the issue or allotment or transfer of shares to or by, a nominee of that company" extends the reference and says nothing of other persons
    WHEN `s 616(2) some other act` THEN
        NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection extends the references in (a) and (b) only

-- src:8278 | The reference in section 611 to the transferor company shall be read accordingly.
@ref s 616(2) Interpretation of this Chapter: the transferor company (src:8278)
GIVEN `the transfer of the non-cash assets is by a nominee of the transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(2) the reference in section 611 to the transferor company is read as including a nominee` MEANS
    IF `the transfer of the non-cash assets is by a nominee of the transferor company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall be read accordingly" extends the reference to a nominee and says nothing of anyone else

-- src:8279 | (3) References in this Chapter to the transfer of shares in a company include the transfer of a right to be included in the company's register of members ... in respect of those shares.
@ref s 616(3) Interpretation of this Chapter: transfer of shares includes transfer of the right to be registered (src:8279)
GIVEN `it is a transfer of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a transfer of a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 616(3) the transaction is a transfer of shares in the company for this Chapter` MEANS
    IF `it is a transfer of shares in the company` OR `it is a transfer of a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" does not close the list
